Falsifies `paging::domain::the_grant_enumeration_is_total`.

The defect: the index-to-offset multiply goes back to a bare one. Every caller in this tree
passes an `i` below the page count, so nothing observable changes and the multiply cannot
overflow on any grant the frame allocator could produce, which is exactly what makes the bare
form look reasonable. `grant_page` is nonetheless a public function over two attacker-shaped
`u64`s, and totality is the property this harness exists for: a panic in the enumeration is a
kernel panic, reached through whatever caller eventually passes an index it did not derive from
`grant_pages`.

Expected to fail: `attempt to multiply with overflow`, at `let off = i * PAGE_SIZE;`, for any
`i` above `u64::MAX / 4096`. The harness body is two calls and no assertions, so a panic is the
only thing in it that can fail and there is nothing else to fail first.

The `grant_pages` half of the harness is untouched here; the `a_grant_the_domain_cannot_express_
is_refused` record breaks that one.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/domain.rs b/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
--- a/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
